[{"id":2361022298,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Mulda","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"07a413912d99a58c88c41620f939be7212bd8e3b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?u=1b0467024f137e562b21748eb6bf12f97dfa5bf6&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","login":"raulsntos","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos"},"body":"It's fine for the exported APK to include the same `.jar` multiple times. As I understand it, `.jar` files can only be added to the APK when building the APK so the pre-built export template APK won't care about these `.jar` files that are added later, we already take care of adding the `.jar` file to the export template APK.\r\n\r\nThe problem you are having is likely exclusive to Gradle builds. The Gradle build likely includes these `.jar` files multiple times because `ExportPlugin::add_shared_object` adds the files to the `android/build/libs` directory and the Gradle build will take all the `.jar` files in there without de-duplicating them when building the APK.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98066#pullrequestreview-2361022298","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98066","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-10-10T17:54:59Z"},{"id":2361096248,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Mu3g4","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"07a413912d99a58c88c41620f939be7212bd8e3b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24307049?u=d195784832ed42069d02554c93df52be645c0009&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/TCROC","id":24307049,"node_id":"M